    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23228" root="شهل" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَهْلَةٌ</span></b>  A <i>middle-aged, intelligent</i> woman: an
epithet peculiarly applied to a woman: (S, O, K:)
one says <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِمْرَأَةٌ شَهْلَةٌ كَهْلَةٌ</span>, but not ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجُلٌ شَهْلٌ</span></b> 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَهْلٌ</span>; though IDrd mentions <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَهْلٌ كَهْلٌ</span>. (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And An <i>old</i> woman. (K.)

